The assignments ξ 7→ Aξ and ξ 7→ Bξ are injective. Indeed, equality
of two such matrices gives 1(ξ − ξ′)T = 0, hence ξ = ξ′. Combining this
observation with full spans makes the reflected labels literal.
Theorem 6.2 (Finite-word literal reciprocity). Let ek = (αk, βk), 0 ≤ k <
n, be a finite typed word whose strict homogeneous arrow domains contain
integer seeds. Phase-resolved reflected-inverse reciprocity for every seed and
every prefix holds if and only if, at every edge,
(i) Rαk ∈ EW and is the unique reflected W-selector;
(ii) Rβk ∈ EV and is the unique reflected V -selector; and
(iii) every reflected source, carry, target, and transformed membership row
is strict.
